{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OSS consensus audit (2026-08-13): APPROVED pattern, already merged as 6f37d9495b.\n\nPopular active projects avoid paying production retry/readiness time in deterministic tests. Kubernetes advances a fake clock in delaying-queue tests instead of waiting (kubernetes/kubernetes@52ba901, staging/src/k8s.io/client-go/util/workqueue/delaying_queue_test.go#L30-L56). Tenacity injects a list.append sleeper and asserts the exact logical schedule [1,2,3,3] (jd/tenacity@26f719d, tests/test_tenacity.py#L590-L604). urllib3 mocks time.sleep when testing Retry-After (urllib3/urllib3@52dfb19, test/test_retry.py#L411-L440).\n\nThis remediation follows that consensus with a zero logical budget and an exact one-poll assertion; it preserves the 120s production default and all failure coverage. Tracker cross-check: related readiness/capability tickets were read during RCA; none rejected logical-time test control. The implementation saved 120.4s for the individual test."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786638492515538001,"uuid":"f6b1ffef-f9ba-45cd-b33a-67f7daf54325"}